{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "30189_ippukusuru",
  "headword": "一服する",
  "reading": "いっぷくする",
  "romaji": "ippukusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to take a short break; to have a smoke or a cup of tea",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to take a short break; to pause for a breather",
      "explanation": "To stop work briefly and relax. {一服|いっぷく} literally means one dose or one serving, so the break is typically accompanied by a cigarette or a cup of tea — often implied even when not stated."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30189_ippukusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "ちょっと{一服|いっぷく}しよう。",
      "english": "Let's take a short break.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30189_ippukusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{仕事|しごと}の{合間|あいま}に{一服|いっぷく}する。",
      "english": "I take a breather between tasks.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30189_ippukusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{昼食|ちゅうしょく}のあと、{庭|にわ}に{出|で}て{一服|いっぷく}するのが{父|ちち}の{習慣|しゅうかん}だ。",
      "english": "Going out to the garden for a smoke after lunch is my father's habit.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30189_ippukusuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{荷物|にもつ}を{全部|ぜんぶ}{運|はこ}び{終|お}えてから、みんなでお{茶|ちゃ}を{飲|の}んで{一服|いっぷく}した。",
      "english": "After carrying in all the luggage, we all had tea and took a break.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Slightly old-fashioned and warm in tone, and strongly associated with smokers, though it is used for any short rest. {一服|いっぷく} also works as a plain noun.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一服|いっぷく}{入|い}れる: to take a breather\n- {一服|いっぷく}つける: to light a cigarette\n- ここらで{一服|いっぷく}: time for a break about now\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {休憩|きゅうけい}する: to take a break — neutral and general; the word used at work or school\n- {一息|ひといき}つく: to catch one's breath — emphasizes relief after finishing something demanding",
